{"content":{"blocks":[{"content":[{"text":"Your questions have been answered: \"Architecture fact: a ConversationSummary is always single-source today — it's grouped by one native conversation.id, which belongs to exactly one adapter (codex or claude-code). So a codex→claude→codex chain doesn't produce one summary with mixed producer.source events; hop B (the claude-fabricated session, once really used) is captured as its own all-claude-code conversation, and hop A's original codex reasoning ciphertext never enters it (A's turns were folded to plain text when B was fabricated). Genuine 'carry a 2-hops-back Codex leg's reasoning into a fresh fabrication' requires new code that walks the lineage chain (lineage.parentOf) back to ancestor hops and pulls in their original ledger events. Given that, what should this pass do?\"=\"Per-event gating only, no chain-walk (Recommended)\", \"Given replay is on by default with no gate the user has to opt into, should there be an escape hatch to turn it off?\"=\"Yes, add an opt-out (Recommended)\". You can now continue with these answers in mind.","type":"input_text"}],"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sv8kokGhyRbNwXRrfhpMf3","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"tool_result"},"context":{"branch":"annals-cledger","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"c3695163c63b537b16512f75ec4e386519cd2bd8","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"id":"ev2-5692020c90b2f0e08f8e593894ff67afd45ba3ec9663611988a07d67b4eb3d89","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"type":"system"},"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai","session_id":"9d261764-bb80-489b-a27a-efbf8948150d","source":"codex","source_version":"0.156.1"},"occurred_at":"2026-07-24T06:39:04.017Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.26.0"},"raw":{"data":{"payload":{"call_id":"toolu_01Sv8kokGhyRbNwXRrfhpMf3","output":[{"text":"Your questions have been answered: \"Architecture fact: a ConversationSummary is always single-source today — it's grouped by one native c