{"content":{"blocks":[{"id":"toolu_01Sv8kokGhyRbNwXRrfhpMf3","input":"{\"questions\":[{\"header\":\"Lineage depth\",\"multiSelect\":false,\"options\":[{\"description\":\"Gate replay on each event's own producer.source (not a blanket per-conversation check) so the logic is correct and forward-compatible. But don't build lineage-chain traversal now — today's data model means this is equivalent to the simple codex→codex case in practice. True cross-hop carry-over (reconstructing an ancestor hop's reasoning during re-bridging) becomes a follow-up roadmap item.\",\"label\":\"Per-event gating only, no chain-walk (Recommended)\"},{\"description\":\"When re-bridging a conversation that has ancestors (lineage.parentOf), walk back through the chain, pull each ancestor's own original ledger events (not the folded-text copy), and splice in reasoning from every Codex-origin leg — real multi-hop support, materially more code and more surface for bugs.\",\"label\":\"Build lineage chain-walk now\"}],\"question\":\"Architecture fact: a ConversationSummary is always single-source today — it's grouped by one native conversation.id, which belongs to exactly one adapter (codex or claude-code). So a codex→claude→codex chain doesn't produce one summary with mixed producer.source events; hop B (the claude-fabricated session, once really used) is captured as its own all-claude-code conversation, and hop A's original codex reasoning ciphertext never enters it (A's turns were folded to plain text when B was fabricated). Genuine 'carry a 2-hops-back Codex leg's reasoning into a fresh fabrication' requires new code that walks the lineage chain (lineage.parentOf) back to ancestor hops and pulls in their original ledger events. Given that, what should this pass do?\"},{\"header\":\"Escape hatch\",\"multiSelect\":false,\"options\":[{\"description\":\"A config flag (e.g. `{\\\"reasoning\\\": {\\\"replay\\\": false}}`) and/or a `--no-reasoning-replay` CLI flag. Cheap to add, gives users a lever give