{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Confirmed — nothing in `src/cli.ts` either. Everything about encrypted-reasoning replay in turnbridge exists only as a roadmap note and a standalone probe script; none of it is wired into the actual fabrication path. I have enough to answer.\n\n## Short answer: insufficient, but for a specific, well-scoped reason\n\nconversation-ledger 0.10.0 (`50b8f40`) did its job — it's a real, verified building block. But it only solves the *storage* half. Turnbridge's fabrication pipeline has **zero code touching `reasoning`-kind events**; the roadmap note in `docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:143-169` describes the design intent, it doesn't implement it. Three concrete gaps, in order they'd bite:\n\n**1. `listConversations` never fetches reasoning events at all**\n`src/conversations.ts:40-43` calls `readEvents(repo, { kind: \"conversation_turn\", ... })` — hardcoded to one kind. `reasoning` events never enter a `ConversationSummary` in the first place, regardless of anything downstream.\n\n**2. Even if fetched, `turnContent()` silently drops them**\n`src/types.ts:59-64` requires `content.role` + `content.blocks`. A `reasoning` event's content is `{opaque: true}` (by design — the payload lives in `raw.data`, not `content`). `buildRolloutLines` in `codex.ts:132-134` does `if (!content) continue;`, so these events would be skipped even if step 1 were fixed.\n\n**3. No replay/gating logic exists**\nThe roadmap text is clear on policy — replay a `reasoning` event's `raw.data` only when `event.producer.source` matches the fabrication target (never feed Codex ciphertext to Claude Code) — but no code implements it. `buildRolloutLines` has no branch for `event.kind === \"reasoning\"`, no logic to pull `raw.data` (the verbatim `response_item` line) and splice it in as an actual rollout line rather than folding it through `foldBlock` as text.\n\nThe good news: what conversation-ledger *does* give turnbridge is sufficient raw material for this — `raw.data` is the byte-exact original line (confirmed in `drift.ts:83-107`, `reasoningDraft`), and `conversation.seq` (source line index) is present on both `reasoning` and `conversation_turn` events, so correct interleaving is derivable without extra ledger work. `producer.source` is already recorded per event, so the \"only replay same-CLI-family\" gate doesn't need the still-missing model/provider/CLI-version field either — that gap (noted in the ledger's own roadmap) matters only for finer things, not this gate.\n\nThe actual splice mechanics are proven — `scripts/probe-encrypted-reasoning.mjs` does it manually, by reading a donor rollout file directly and inserting the raw line before the last assistant `response_item`. But that script bypasses turnbridge's event pipeline entirely (reads the rollout file, not the ledger via `ConversationSummary`), so it validates the *provider accepts a replayed blob*, not that *turnbridge can produce one*.\n\n**Net:** conversation-ledger's update is well-designed and not the blocker. What's missing is entirely turnbridge-side: extend `listConversations`/`readEvents` to pull `reasoning` events into the group, extend `ConversationSummary`/`turnContent` (or add a parallel path) so opaque events survive to the target adapter, and add the source-match gate + splice logic in `codex.ts` (and decide whether `claude-code.ts` ever needs a symmetric path, since Claude Code doesn't emit ciphertext reasoning today). None of that exists yet — it's still open work, not a design flaw in what's shipped.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"annals-cledger","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"c3695163c63b537b16512f75ec4e386519cd2bd8","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"id":"ev2-e260b4e2875d67bf7b8a888b6e156182d6921cd6eb2351e621c09c38cdd9f8af","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"type":"agent"},"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai","session_id":"9d261764-bb80-489b-a27a-efbf8948150d","so